 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Dog Breed Quiz Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a dog breed quiz?\", \"a\": \"A dog breed quiz is a short set of questions about your home, schedule, and habits, scored so your answers point to one dog breed. The quiz on this page asks eight questions and names one of five breeds, from Labrador Retriever to French Bulldog.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a dog breed quiz?\", \"a\": \"Decide which breeds the quiz can name, then describe the quiz in a prompt, including what the result screen shows. Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> drafts each question with one option per breed and saves every finished quiz to a database you own. Publish it and share the link.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does a dog breed for me quiz pick one result?\", \"a\": \"It counts which breed your answers point to most often. Each option adds a point to one breed, and the breed with the most points after the last question is your result. If two breeds tie, the quiz needs a rule for which one wins, such as the first breed on its list. A what dog breed am I quiz scores the same way.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a best dog breed for me quiz ask about my home?\", \"a\": \"It should ask about indoor space and the yard, the hours it would spend alone, and how much exercise you can give on a weekday. Weigh those answers above a favorite look. The same idea makes a good <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/style'>style quiz</a>: ask about real choices, not how people see themselves.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many breeds should a dog breed selector quiz include?\", \"a\": \"Five is a workable number for an eight-question quiz. Each question then holds one option per breed without running past a phone screen. Add a breed only when you add a question, and each breed keeps a fair path to win. On Emergent, adding a sixth breed later is one follow-up prompt.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can a dog breed personality quiz help a pet brand grow its email list?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if the email is optional and the result comes first. Put the offer on the result screen, such as breed care tips by email, and ask for nothing before it. Emergent sets no response caps, and a quiz shared widely records every result.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can an ultimate dog breed quiz mix trivia with breed matching?\", \"a\": \"Yes, as long as the two parts are scored separately. Trivia questions have one right answer and a score, the way a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/vocabulary'>vocabulary quiz</a> does, while matching questions add points to a breed. Put the trivia round last. The breed match then never depends on how many facts someone knows.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a dog breed quiz ask for an email before showing the result?\", \"a\": \"No. Show the result first and ask for the email after, as an option with a clear reason, like a care checklist for that breed. Keep the email field optional. Nobody should have to sign up to see a match. Each address someone does give lands in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a what dog breed are you quiz the same as a genetic breed test?\", \"a\": \"No. A what dog breed are you quiz matches a person to a breed from their answers about home and habits. It says nothing about the ancestry of a dog you already own. Keep the two apart in your copy, and never word a quiz result as if it describes a real dog's breed mix.\"}, {\"q\": \"Where should a pet startup put its dog breed quiz?\", \"a\": \"Give it a page of its own and link that page from the home page and from every social post that mentions the quiz. Look at the <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-landing-page-builder/startup'>best startup landing pages</a> for layout ideas, then put one action above the fold: starting the quiz. Keep the first question visible without scrolling on a phone.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
